  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Operational Foresight and Supporting Local Preparedness in the Context of Climate Displacement, Fiji; Indonesia; Philippines; Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving data related to potential future climate displacement is critical to advancing targeted, context-specific responses that integrate both short and long-term perspectives, and improving understanding of the phenomenon beyond environmental factors, including political, economic, sociocultural, and demographic drivers of displacement. To support this improved evidence base, IOM and its partners are proposing this pilot action, targeting the Philippines, Indonesia, Thailand and Fiji, to (1) Create a Risk Index for Climate Displacement (RICD) which will improve understanding of potential future impacts on population movements and underpin local action and integrate RICD data into local contingency and DRRM planning processes; (2) Catalyse local finance and action to implement priority actions identified during the planning process, through the creation of a Climate Catalytic Fund (CCF). CCF actions will enhance resilience and prevention efforts, principally through an HDPN approach; (3) Support immediate response in case of new crises.</narrative>
  </description>
